{"author":{"id":"6d85cf2fcebaeefd8c5c528f2d5f5f98f26ce3275422d0dc5f7c0fd596f9f59f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791729658,"nonce":"BaVSmYev3/sGjQQH1wl5gwKLZ4g=","title":"text-overflow: ellipsis","message":"A line of text that overflows the block container asking for it ends with an ellipsis: text-overflow is read as a paint write and kept per node (Tree::text_overflows, set through LayoutContext::set_text_overflow), and the paint walk finds the nearest ancestor with an entry, measures the room from the text's left edge to that container's content edge (its own width when less), and when the shaped line is wider re-shapes the longest start of the text followed by U+2026 that fits, found by halving. The glyphs' ink is allowed an eighth of the font size past the advance layout measures by. A text of several lines is left to line-clamp. Measurement is unchanged: a shrink-to-fit box is still as wide as the whole text, as in CSS, so the container's own width decides. Selection and textContent are untouched, as the shaping is only for drawing.","files":null}]}